s plinth by the court; the garden to the south: the long central lawn between gravel walks and alleys of limes, the bosquets either side, the round basin and the hedged hemicycle at the far end; the garden wall. Guessed: all dimensions, the window rhythm, the garden's exact layout; the house's orientation is taken with the court to the north."}